=== Prompt 4 ===
Enhance the agent to operate in two distinct modes:
1. Interactive mode: The agent and the user exchange information. The agent can ask the user questions, and the user fills in gaps and determines the direction of exploration. The agent can also provide clarifications and additional context or background if it semantically and dynamically detects that some details might not be well covered or are unclear, or that there could be an opportunity for slippery, potentially dangerous, and highly incorrect inferences based on interpretations of different parts and a lack of evidence or facts.
2. Batch (headless, non-interactive) mode: Suitable for running the agent on multiple inputs, for example, to process a whole batch or series of support cases without a user present. In this mode, the agent must carefully check whether it can make the necessary conclusions based solely on the inputs it has been provided. If it cannot, it must abort its operation and emit a suitable message explaining why it decided to terminate its run. This termination decision should happen on a case-by-case basis. If the agent is processing a batch of whatever number of cases, it must not abort the whole batch if it turns out that only one particular support case lacks the necessary data or clarity, details, confidence, etc.
